{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1540112-faster-human-healing","id":1540112,"title":"Faster Human Healing","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-08-09T17:41:52-07:00","id":1540112,"title":"Faster Human Healing","content":"I'm planning to create a short adventure with my player being basic humans. They will be detectives and police officers investigating on a series of murders. Naturally the murderer will be a vampire, and since they will have to stop him they'll surely be hurt (or killed) and will have to chase him maybe over several nights<br /> <br /> In VTM and WTA source book it is said that it need (lot of) time to heal, but it may be a bit too long. I would like to houserule something to let them heal lethal damage at a rate of 1 per days. I'm not saying they will completely heal, their health box will be clear but they will suffer long time injuries and disabilities (Speed divided by 2, impossibility to run, increased difficulty for some actions, less dice to roll or worse)<br /> <br /> My first idea is:<br /> -Before rolling to speed up the healing there has to be a roll to stabilize the wounded character, so that he can move without aggravating his injuries. The difficulty should be vary (maybe 6 for bruised to injured, 7 for wounded and mauled, 8 for crippled and 9 for inacapcitated), the st can ask multiple success to stabilize critical injuries, using medical supply can lower the difficulty by 1 or 2 at the st discretion. Only after that you can roll to speed up the healing<br /> <br /> -Intelligence + Medicine difficulty 8, if the roll is a success the worst wound will heal in 1 day. To heal quickly, the character must be treated like this every day, each time allowing to heal the actual health box in 1 day.<br /> <br /> -The difficulty is increased by 1 if a character try to heal hismelf (unless incapacitated of course)<br /> <br /> Yeah i know depending on the vampire's powers and age it's possible they have no chance at all, the purpose of this short story is to be an horrific one, where they will know any mistake could be fatal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","name":"Cain Loup-Noir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26839_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-09T19:05:52-07:00","id":1540115,"title":"","content":"That sounds like more bookkeeping and rolls than necessary for what you're aiming.<br /> <br /> First, be sure they understand how dangerous any wound is. Any confrontation can lead to a dead character, to the point that healing may end up being irrelevant.<br /> <br /> Second, keep it descriptive. Adding penalties and disabilities will just undo any benefit from giving them better healing. Health levels are just a mechanic to say how far you're from death, you may be beaten and full of injuries and yet be good to go again.<br /> <br /> Each time a character gets damage, let them roll Stamina. If they fail, they need medical attention. Dif 5-7, it's more luck than anything, if the character is incapacitated they also need equipped paramedics to be moved.<br /> <br /> I suggest this rule because it adds drama, but it's just a single roll. You can write in their sheets the difficulty along each Health Box and let the players engage with the rule. A hidden advantage is that if the enemy knows you're in no condition of giving chase, they can let you go.<br /> <br /> Other than that, just let them heal. You can add an artifact or ritual for healing, or maybe it's just the wonders of state of the art medicine, or even it's just how things are, again, Health Boxes aren't about actual health or injury, they're just about staying alive.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-10T01:25:42-07:00","id":1540122,"title":"","content":"If i understand correctly, you roll stamina and on a fail you need mediacl attention wich means that you don't touch your actual checked health box but with some medical treatment you can cancel the effect of your health situation ? <br /> <br /> Like if you're wounded and you're healed you don't suffer the -2 dice and movement penalty ?<br /> <br /> The idea is a good one, but it's precisely the fact of moving away from death that means that in the event of multiple confrontations spread over several days, a character can be wounded several times without being guaranteed to die.<br /> <br /> The artifact or ritual won't be of any use because they will be playing character who are unaware of the supernatural, they will discover it the hard way in this short story","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","name":"Cain Loup-Noir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26839_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-10T02:36:58-07:00","id":1540123,"title":"","content":"Is there a reason to send them after a fully stated VtM vampire that is such a dangerous threat to them? I know that combat tuning in the WoD is not simple, but a vampire killer does not have to be a serious threat in a stand up fight against prepared humans. Your average 0 XP starting level vampire that's not built for a real fight (instead of isolating and killing humans in a controlled fashion where they can stack things in their favor) is by no means guaranteed to be putting a bunch of cops in the hospital for months at a time even with the normal rules in place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-10T08:48:32-07:00","id":1540131,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1540112-faster-human-healing?p=1540123#post1540123\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there a reason to send them after a fully stated VtM vampire that is such a dangerous threat to them? I know that combat tuning in the WoD is not simple, but a vampire killer does not have to be a serious threat in a stand up fight against prepared humans. Your average 0 XP starting level vampire that's not built for a real fight (instead of isolating and killing humans in a controlled fashion where they can stack things in their favor) is by no means guaranteed to be putting a bunch of cops in the hospital for months at a time even with the normal rules in place.</div> </div> </div> </div>The vampire will not be very old, just what it take to be stronger than humans and a big threat to the party. A Brujah with 5 points to be divided between his 3 Disciplines. His regular pool will be like 6/5/3 (stronger pool without Celerity or Potence to the weakest). Without Fortitude and a Stamina of 4 against 3 pc with pistols (and better at the end if they call the contact i'll give to one of them).<br /> <br /> The reason the Vampire leave such a trail behind him is because he's loosing his fight agaisnt the beast, his murder are ugly, full of bites clearly unnatural. The main weakness of that vampire is that he's a coward, he fear final death more than anything and will more likely try to escape the party than actively trying to kill them, and that make the possibility of multiple encounter very likely, hence the need for a faster healing system for the human pc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","name":"Cain Loup-Noir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26839_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-10T11:36:35-07:00","id":1540134,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cain Loup-Noir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1540112-faster-human-healing?p=1540122#post1540122\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If i understand correctly, you roll stamina and on a fail you need mediacl attention wich means that you don't touch your actual checked health box but with some medical treatment you can cancel the effect of your health situation ?</div> </div> </div> </div>No, my idea is that with a failed roll the wound is bleeding or whatever, and the character needs attention for things to not get worse.<br /> <br /> Basically, on a failed roll the character is out of combat. If they're with a penalty, first aid is probably enough. If they're incapacitated, then you need to call an ambulance. If the PC insists on taking actions the injury worsen, but if they wait for help there's no need to track time or even to roll for the medical attention, as long as it is adequate. Adjust as you see fit.<br /> <br /> Tracking injuries separately from damage will just add a lot of extra bookkeeping, as their effect is basically the same as what damage penalties already do. Worse, it will reduce their ability to succeed as time goes on, which basically stacks the odds even more against them.<br /> <br /> Use the Stamina Roll to add the spice of implying greater consequences without really reducing their chances at survival. Don't roll for the actual medical attention, just require adequate equipment. Let them heal 1 lethal a day without added problems.<br /> <br /> You only need to complicate things if a character is without access to a clean bed and needed medical supplies. And if you want the grit realism of a normal human going against terrible odds, then more important than the healing rate is the quality of attention the injury receives. A vampire killer that gets hit hard shouldn't be in a position to refuse going to the hospital.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-10T18:12:56-07:00","id":1540159,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cain Loup-Noir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1540112-faster-human-healing?p=1540131#post1540131\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The vampire will not be very old, just what it take to be stronger than humans and a big threat to the party.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's.. sorta the problem I have though. Why make it such a &quot;big threat to the party&quot; that you need to house rules the Health rules to keep the game on track? You've already set it up so that the vampire is a coward that is likely to flee over fighting three armed humans prepared to fight. So why is there any serious risk of damage until they finally corner it for the fight at the end where the vampire is finally stuck with no choice?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-12T06:21:32-07:00","id":1540200,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1540112-faster-human-healing?p=1540159#post1540159\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's.. sorta the problem I have though. Why make it such a &quot;big threat to the party&quot; that you need to house rules the Health rules to keep the game on track? You've already set it up so that the vampire is a coward that is likely to flee over fighting three armed humans prepared to fight. So why is there any serious risk of damage until they finally corner it for the fight at the end where the vampire is finally stuck with no choice?</div> </div> </div> </div>Cause i've seen some unlucky roll lately x) some botch or fail in a situation where pc had the upper hand and yet rolled multiple 1 and failed to dodge. Not so terrible since it was in a wta campaign they healed quickly but in the case of humans character losing 2 health level considering their healing rate in the books is already a terrible.<br /> <br /> Anyway as said earlier that Brujah will have 5 dots to divide between his disciplines, i'll run some test before launching the story to be sure it work as intended. If you have any advice on the clan or power level of a vampire ennemy against a human group in an horror like story i'm happy to take<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5826_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5826\" data-vbnamecard=\"5826\">monteparnas</a> So i let them heal 1 lethal per days for as long as they receive appropriate medical attention, and if they're injured during the story they roll stamina to know if they can keep up or are badly wounded.<br /> <br /> I apply the wound penalty in the 2 case an if the stamina roll fail give a major injury to the pc, if he decide to go on it get worse (bigger penalty and/or more damage). Is that right?<br /> And if they receive a bad injury after a failed stamina and are healed, do you think they should keep a longer bad effect or disable it for as long as they're precautious in their actions?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26839,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","user":"Cain Loup-Noir","date":". 08-12-2024, 09:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","name":"Cain Loup-Noir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26839_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-12T15:13:18-07:00","id":1540225,"title":"","content":"That's correct.<br /> <br /> After healing it's best to have no aftereffects even if they failed the Stamina Roll. Ongoing penalties would undo the benefits of the system.<br /> <br /> Your selection of Clan and Disciplines will depend upon which kind of horror you want to enact. Assuming you want the basic feeling of &quot;this is a superhuman threat&quot;, I would keep Brujah and make it Potence 2, Celerity 2, Presence 1.<br /> <br /> Presence is a good way to hit the PC's Willpower, don't worry about how easy it is to shrug off. Also, it works on NPCs, which means the group will quickly learn they can't face this enemy in a crowd.<br /> <br /> In fact, uses of Presence are a good way to establish that something isn't right. You can use it a lot without it being a terrible risk to the players.<br /> <br /> But mostly I think <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a> has a point. You're worrying a lot about possible damage before their actual confrontation, when you already established that this guy (or gal) is a coward.<br /> <br /> Sure, with Presence and Animalism you <b>can</b> have your players getting into physical confrontations because of the vampire, without them being with the vampire. But as I see the situation, both parties will only get down and dirty at the last moment possible, unless the players are really bad at solving anything without their fists.<br /> <br /> My ideal scenario for such a story would be to have any reason to establish the vampire will avoid confrontation, and the victory condition be staking them during the day. In fact you can roll such a story with even stronger vampires as long as you don't expect the players to be dumb enough to go face to face.<br /> <br /> With a full rules VtM vampire, players need brain, not better healing. Have the vampire show off a little, or even a lot, in their view, so they know that a physical confrontation is a bad idea. Have the vampire notice the group if things get tense, so the coward flees pronto.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-12T15:56:36-07:00","id":1540233,"title":"","content":"Bumping Presence high gets you Dread Gaze and the ability to send PCs running temporarily without having to fight as another option in the &quot;avoid damage to avoid the problems of mortals healing,&quot; issue.<br /> <br /> There's also just... sticking to Bashing damage as much as possible. Mortals can heal up from incapacitated with Bashing to fully healthy in a bit over a days worth of rest. Until lethal weapons start getting used (or the vampire is trying to do grapple-bites, but that's a reason to avoid too much Potence), the healing times aren't that harsh. Celerity to punch them all hard enough to inflict stun before running away is going to be a few hours of rest... so punch instead of stab.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-12T17:22:13-07:00","id":1540242,"title":"","content":"I don't think grapple would be seen as an option by this vampire when facing several opponents. It does come with making yourself vulnerable to others for a while.<br /> <br /> Even if this isn't as harsh as it sounds, the character don't need to know the rules well. The sensation of vulnerability may be more than enough to discourage such tactic, again removing risks of excessive lethality.<br /> <br /> At the same time, judicious (or not so much) use of Potence for the automatic successes is a way to both intimidate PCs and drain the Blood Pool to the chosen level.<br /> <br /> By the way, that's a thing: for this scenario it's good to keep track of the vampire's Blood Pool. Have a target for how much Blood they should have at key encounters, specially the first and final confrontations, but track the pool to see if the PCs are able to hinder their replenishments in some way.<br /> <br /> Remember that even a 13th Gen can bump all Physical attributes to 6 for a scene and become far more dangerous than normal if put in a tight situation with a full pool. At the same time, a vampire killer can have a far easier job if their target is mostly spent at the end.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-12T17:59:14-07:00","id":1540246,"title":"","content":"Lethal damage was a potential problem since i haven't decide what kind of weapon the brujah will use to defend himself. A pistol (without any full magazine left in his pocket except the one loaded) or knife.<br /> The knife fit with the savage influence of the beast though, the gun was related to the brujah backstory. Since a Vampire with celerity can take multiple action in a round, i feared the case where the pc's try to ambush him and the creature has to face one of them to escape.<br /> <br /> I could also decide he does not have any weapons at all at the beggining and the pc have to act smart to prevent him getting any or use anything to dangerous.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","name":"Cain Loup-Noir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26839_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-12T18:03:46-07:00","id":1540249,"title":"","content":"The grapple-bite is a specific thing because it's the only free lethal/agg damage vampires get as a natural weapon instead of having to use a weapon or buy a power. A Potence 5 grapple and bite is pretty much a guaranteed one-shot fatal wound on a mortal.<br /> <br /> But yeah, there is math and there's psychology at play here.<br /> <br /> A modified example from a VtR 1e campaign of mine:<br /> <br /> We were playing a human-to-ghoul-to-vampire game. While still human, the PCs got introduced to one of the main antagonists who took out an already established combat powerhouse vampire in a single hit. What they didn't know (partially because it was a home brewed thing I made), is that the enemy in question got major buffs depending on how low a target's Morality/etc. trait was, and it was even more powerful against things not on Morality at all. Said combat powerhouse was sitting at Humanity 3, and got crubstomped because of that effect. The PCs not knowing this, took a lot of time to find out that as Morality 6-7 ghouls (by that point) they were basically just fighting a guy using simple weapons, and until they finally pieced it all together, they avoided combat like they were fighting an insanely high XP opponent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-13T06:41:15-07:00","id":1540270,"title":"","content":"Grapple-Bite is my second source of dangerous damage in that story after the weapon, but unless the pc split to find the vampire or just looking for something without knowing he's hidden somewhere it's very unlikely they end grapple-bited.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5826_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5826\" data-vbnamecard=\"5826\">monteparnas</a> when they receive appropriate healing, would you let them go around and still heal or would you make them they need to rest somewhere safe to heal (hospital, at home in their bed...)?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","name":"Cain Loup-Noir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26839_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-13T12:39:16-07:00","id":1540281,"title":"","content":"Whatever flows for the story, at that point.<br /> <br /> Overall the nearer someone is to being fully healed, the less they need intense care. But putting too strict rules on that risks a situation where you have just boring waiting for no dramatic payoff.<br /> <br /> Injury and healing is insanely more complex and varied irl than any system can really hope to emulate. Being out of the hospital in a couple days after being seemingly mauled in a car crash? That happens.<br /> <br /> My point is, realism has nothing to do with this, hence why I said to keep things descriptive. Keep the PCs out of action the time the story needs.<br /> <br /> By the way, they'll probably avoid doing much while injured due to the penalties, so it may never be an issue. If at any point they want to rise and take their chances, let them do so.<br /> <br /> You can even compromise on the middle. Maybe they can take some actions, but need to go back to care after a while. Maybe some actions are possible, but others aren't. And maybe doing certain things injured take more time. Whatever feels more compelling at the moment.<br /> <br /> Now, I really don't suggest this vampire being armed at first. Between the extra Strength and the possible automatic successes, even Potence 1 is enough to make a vampire into a powerhouse compared to the average human. And since for most people strength is relatively visible, it's easy for the coward predator to only target the meek.<br /> <br /> So think about it. This monster don't need any weapon most of the time, only the Kiss. You already established that the reaction to danger is flight, never confrontation. All a knife will do is raise eyebrows for absolutely no benefit. Don't think about the fight you, the ST, know will happen. Think about what this character needs in their life.<br /> <br /> And of course, lots of people carry knifes, it's not a big deal and is concealable. But lots of people don't, and we're not trying to justify the knife, taking it out at the start is best.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-13T16:40:16-07:00","id":1540311,"title":"","content":"Precise and usefull as always guys, thanks for the help <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","name":"Cain Loup-Noir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26839_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-14T10:47:59-07:00","id":1540370,"title":"","content":"I was learning about the Call of Cthulhu module Horror on the Orient Express, and I guess it is a common houserule for that module that players should make a character sheet for a 'friend' or 'attendant' or other character who would make sense to be 'read-in' on a moments notice who would also be invested in the story. The idea is that, in that system, injuries are long lasting and death is easy to come by so in the story which is time-constrained and geography-constrained to one particular train trip, it is important to have characters waiting in the wings to tag-in as necessary.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27296-devidramoth","name":"Devidramoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27296_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}